  "description": "What Our Experts Are Saying:\n\n\"I can't think of a better rig to explore the great outdoors than the Nishiki Colorado! This bike is kitted out with a 2 X 8 MicroShift drivetrain for superior offroad shifting, front and rear mechanical disc brakes for improved stopping power and an SR Suntour XCT30 suspension fork with 100mm of travel to smooth out even the roughest terrain. Put simply, this hardtail RIPS!\" - Rich, Regional Bike Leader at DICK'S Sporting Goods Clay, NY\n\nManufacturer may substitute components with components of equal or greater performance level\n\nA perfect bike for when you head outdoors! The Nishiki Colorado Mountain Bike delivers a smooth ride over trails and rough roads thanks to its lightweight and agile alloy frame that uses 100mm of travel on the front suspension fork. It features a pro-grade Microshift 2 x 8 speed drive train that delivers a reliable performance on both flat and hilly terrain. Mechanical disc brakes deliver great control over wet and dry conditions. This mountain bike provides wider, lightweight double wall aluminum 27.5/29\" multi terrain off-road tires for solid traction. This bike takes you anywhere, through trails or around town!\n\nFeatures:\n\nAdult performance mountain bike\n\nLightweight 6061 aluminum frame with tapered head tube, internal cables, dropper post ready, replaceable derailleur hanger\n\nSturdy aluminum construction offers long-term durability\n\nMechanical disc brakes offer reliable stopping power\n\nLightweight double wall aluminum rims with 27.5/29” x 2.35” multi-terrain tires offer reliable stopping power\n\nComfortable SR/Suntour XCT30 suspension fork with 100mm travel\n\nMicroShift 2 x 8 speed drivetrain helps to provide smooth and efficient gear changes\n\nBike weighs approximately 34 lbs.",
